# Feature QA Test Cases

When implementing a new feature, create a QA test-case markdown file before considering the work complete.

## Required for every feature

1. **Create a test-case file** in the same change.
2. **Cover** happy path, validation errors, auth/permission boundaries, and money/edge cases.
3. **Hand off to QA** — this file is what QA runs.

## File location

```
docs/qa/<feature-name>.test-cases.md
```

Kebab-case matching the feature (e.g. `release-payslip.test-cases.md`).

## Template

```markdown
# [Feature Name] — QA Test Cases

## Overview

Where to find it (route, hook, HRIS endpoint).

## Prerequisites

- Role / permissions
- Test data (pay run, employee)

## Test Cases

### TC-01: [Short title]

- **Priority:** High | Medium | Low
- **Preconditions:** ...
- **Steps:**
  1. ...
- **Expected result:** ...

## Edge Cases & Error States

- ...

## Out of Scope

- ...
```

## Minimum coverage

- [ ] Happy path
- [ ] Validation / error states
- [ ] Auth or role restrictions
- [ ] Money / empty list / loading if relevant

## Same-change requirements

1. Feature doc under `docs/`
2. This QA file
3. Clean `pnpm typecheck` (and lint)

Do not add Playwright/RTL/`*.test.tsx`. Manual browser QA uses this markdown.
